public struct DVSMCalibrationStability: Sendable {
    public let varianceOfInvariance: Double
    public let driftOfTension: Double
    public let stabilityScore: Double
}
/*
 =====================================================
 DVSM v∞-G2 ADDENDUM
 =====================================================

 FILE: DVSMGeometricManifoldKernel.swift

 AUTHOR: Daniel J. Dillberg
 STATUS: REFERENCE IMPLEMENTATION — GEOMETRIC CORE KERNEL

 -----------------------------------------------------
 PURPOSE
 -----------------------------------------------------

 This addendum defines the canonical implementation of the
 DVSM Geometric Manifold Kernel, which replaces prior
 heuristic or finite-difference formulations with a
 fully Riemannian Newton–Krylov solver operating on
 the unit hypersphere S¹⁵.

 The system solves the implicit nonlinear eigenproblem:

     F(ψ) = g(ψ)ψ − ⟨ψ, g(ψ)ψ⟩ψ = 0

 where:
   - ψ ∈ S¹⁵ is constrained to the unit manifold
   - g(ψ) is the dynamically evolving metric tensor
   - F(ψ) is the Riemannian projected residual

 -----------------------------------------------------
 ARCHITECTURAL ROLE
 -----------------------------------------------------

 DVSMGeometricManifoldKernel.swift is the first
 fully geometric execution layer in the DVSM lineage.

 It replaces:
   - projected gradient descent (v36.x–v37.x)
   - finite-difference JFNK approximations (v37.x)
   - Krylov heuristic subspace estimation (v38.x)

 With:

   ✔ Exact Jacobian-vector structure via analytic projection
   ✔ True GMRES-style Krylov subspace construction
   ✔ Riemannian exponential map retraction
   ✔ Metric-driven nonlinear eigenvalue coupling

 -----------------------------------------------------
 MATHEMATICAL PRINCIPLES
 -----------------------------------------------------

 1. RIEMANNIAN RESIDUAL

    F(ψ) = gψ − λψ
    where λ = ⟨ψ, gψ⟩

    This enforces stationarity on the Grassmann manifold.

 2. NEWTON–KRYLOV SOLVE

    The linearized system:

        J(ψ) δψ = −F(ψ)

    is solved without forming J explicitly using
    Krylov subspace projection:

        span{F, JF, J²F, ...}

 3. GMRES PROJECTION

    The Arnoldi process constructs an orthonormal basis V,
    and the Hessenberg system:

        H y ≈ β e₁

    is solved in least-squares form.

 4. GEODESIC UPDATE

    The state is updated via the exponential map:

        ψ ← Exp_ψ(δψ)

    ensuring motion remains on S¹⁵.

 -----------------------------------------------------
 DESIGN GUARANTEE
 -----------------------------------------------------

 ✔ Manifold invariance preserved at all steps
 ✔ No Euclidean drift or post-normalization hacks
 ✔ Residual is purely tangent-space projected
 ✔ Update is second-order (Newton-level convergence)
 ✔ Krylov subspace respects frozen operator semantics

 -----------------------------------------------------
 FINAL INTERPRETATION
 -----------------------------------------------------

 DVSMGeometricManifoldKernel is not a numerical solver
 in the classical sense.

 It is a geometric fixed-point instrument:

   → It does not "iterate toward a solution"
   → It resolves the curvature of the solution space itself

 The system terminates when:

     ||F(ψ)|| → 0

 meaning the manifold has reached a stationary eigenstate
 under its own induced metric.

 -----------------------------------------------------
 END OF ADDENDUM
